# #38 (docs/phase-nav-brief.md, "C: verification"): D6's reveal/split
# stub ("ship UI_T_REVEAL as a push stub marked (warning), ... UI_T_SPLIT
# is likewise a push stub until Phase 7"). The round-trip itself (kind
# recorded and mirrored on pop for all three kinds, and all five D7
# duration values) is already a host test: tests/nav/test_nav.c
# test_transitions(), committed with the #38 contracts -- it is exact and
# needs no UI script. Nothing in this phase's menu wiring ever calls
# ui_push_t(..., UI_T_REVEAL) or UI_T_SPLIT) though (D6: "Its only caller,
# Extras > Clocks, is itself a stub this phase" -- Extras has no
# sub-items at all yet, just ui_stub_screen), so there is no UI path to
# exercise the *runtime* stub behaviour end to end. This script is the
# closest proxy and a regression baseline for when Extras grows a real
# Clocks item: Extras pushes today exactly like any other split -> full
# push (D7: 250 ms in, 290 ms out; 8b-4a: the parting plus its 120 ms
# header bar, 370 and 410), the same generic motion a real
# UI_T_REVEAL would also get in v1 (ui_main.c does not special-case the
# kind). When Extras > Clocks becomes real and wires UI_T_REVEAL, this
# script's "Extras is still a plain push" assumption needs revisiting.
# P12 W1-F: Extras is now the split Extras list (a split -> split push,
# 190 ms each way) and Extras > Clocks is the UI_T_REVEAL caller
# (extras_table); W1-C's real Clocks screen (the world map and analog
# clock, full width, no panel) is the reveal target, a push in v1:
# split -> full: 250 in (D7); the pop back to the split list measures
# 240 (D7 says 290: flagged to the nav owner, P12 W1-F report).
# P12 W2-W: Clocks is real and the reveal is wired (ui_main.c, the
# measured motion of nav_reveal_offsets(): the map stays, the list and
# the panel's clock leave left, the band comes in), 250 ms each way;
# ipodui-p12-clocks-reveal records its frames.
#   SIM_BUILD=build/sim-ui scripts/shots.sh tests/ui/ipodui-nav-reveal.script
# golden: skip push_mid pop_mid
# log: reveal start dir=1
# log: reveal start dir=-1
# transitions: 190 250 250 190

wait 4000           # boot to the main menu, "Music" selected

wheel +2             # "Extras" (3rd main-menu row)
wait 400
key SELECT 50
wait 700             # the Extras list (split), "Clocks" selected
key SELECT 50        # Clocks: UI_T_REVEAL
shot push_mid        # (timing) sliding in
wait 700
shot extras          # the Clocks page, no header, no panel

key MENU 50
shot pop_mid         # (timing) sliding back
wait 700
key MENU 50          # the Extras list, then the main menu
wait 700
shot back

quit
